A signature is the "decryption" of the message with the private key: **S = M^d mod n**.

```c
BN_hex2bn(&M1, "<hex of I owe you $2000.>");   // python3 -c 'print("I owe you $2000.".encode().hex())'
BN_mod_exp(S1, M1, d, n, ctx);
BN_hex2bn(&M2, "<hex of I owe you $3000.>");
BN_mod_exp(S2, M2, d, n, ctx);
```

```
~/rsa-lab/unlock.sh 4 <S1> <S2>
```
